zed that while i  have done very little in spanish  my spanish is over the last say 20 years  i was here for my 50th birthday and i  had trouble communicating in spanish and  i remember that i bought a book  and it was the first book i had ever  read in spanish and i remember that  there were many words there that i  didn't know and that was one of the  motivations for getting into link  because i got tired of looking words up  making a list and never remembering  anything  so  that's  whatever it is 24 years ago  and here i am today having interviews  and my spanish is better than it was  then i understand better i'm speaking  fluently with mistakes but more fluently  so i'm thinking to myself why is that  and i'm increasingly convinced that it's  the fact that i have been learning so  many languages in the last  12 years i've learned  or worked at  11 languages  and so i am more fit my brain is more  fit for language learning so i am better  at language learning than i was  50 years ago i'm better at these  languages even languages that i haven't  worked at i am better at them and so  therefore the issue of language learning  is not a matter of learning the theory  like people here in spain they learn one  language essentially english like we do  in canada in the english school system  they learn french and you just keep on  trying to learn that language and you  feel you're not making progress and a  majority of people give up and convince  themselves they can't learn  and then we look at sweden where they  have  the  english language and other foreign  language television programs in the  original language as was the case in  croatia where english language skills  are very good  so then you say well all right then  first of all people say well in sweden  sweden is similar to english therefore  they learn but in croatia it's not  similar to english the pronunciation is  not similar to english nothing is  similar and yet there again they speak  with very little accent and they speak  very well so i believe that it's this  idea that they have the original version  of movies and television programs but  it's not just that this helps them learn  english  it's that this makes them more language  fit  it exposes them as kids initially to  different languages different sounds  different ways of saying things this  means then that when they go to learn  say english focus in on some of the  grammar acquires  words they're more capable of doing it  they notice things better they have a a  context  they're first of all they're they're  comfortable with the idea that they're  listening to things that they don't  really understand that well and they  manage to somehow gradually understand  more and more so this uncertainty which  is sort of accepting uncertainty which  is so important for language learning is  something that the kids acquire by  watching cartoons in strange languages  so the idea of exposing yourself to a  language and in my case learning a  number of languages makes me a better  language learner why is it that  polyglots can go from speaking three  languages to speaking eight languages  because with each language their brain  becomes more fit  so if i look at particularly the last  four or five languages where i've used  our mini stories  the many stories is like a  like a health club it's like a fitness  club it's where you start getting that  fitness you start in the middle of the  language you don't start with the colors  and the numbers and the names of the  members of your family and how are you  and that kind of you just start in a  simple context with lots of repetition  and that way you kind of train yourself  in the language and at some point you  graduate to netflix and all these other  good things that are available on the  internet  so the theory then of languages and  perhaps the way languages should be  taught  is to forget the idea of worrying about  accuracy you know if i was in a  bookstore here and i 